# Runtime dependencies — SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# Edit this file, never requirements.txt. requirements.txt is a fully-pinned
# lockfile compiled from this one; the Dockerfile and CI install from the lock
# so every build gets byte-identical dependencies.
#
# Regenerate after editing (targets 3.12 to match backend/Dockerfile and CI,
# NOT whatever Python you have locally):
#
#     cd backend
#     uv pip compile --python-version 3.12 requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#     uv pip compile --python-version 3.12 requirements-dev.in -o requirements-dev.txt
#
# Commit requirements.in and both lockfiles together.

fastapi
uvicorn
plaid-python
python-dotenv
arq
sqlalchemy[asyncio]
asyncpg
alembic
cryptography
bcrypt
PyJWT
httpx
email-validator
slowapi
# Pinned to 5.x by arq, which hard-requires redis[hiredis]<6. redis cannot move
# to 6+ without replacing arq (it runs the durable job queue: Plaid webhooks,
# manual sync, the alert cron). redis-py 8 also defaults to the RESP3 wire
# protocol, so it is a real migration, not a version bump. Leave this alone —
# the resolver enforces the ceiling via arq, no explicit pin needed here.
redis
groq
pyotp
boto3  # AWS KMS envelope encryption for secrets at rest
# Observability
sentry-sdk[fastapi]
prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator
opentelemetry-sdk
opentelemetry-instrumentation-fastapi
opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-grpc
